quired": false, "is_grouped_calendar": false, "is_free_allowed": true, "is_no_tax": true, "sortable_index": 15250, "description": "## About\nExplore Boston City Hall with Boston By Foot on a free guided tour!  Whether you love its striking brutalist design or think it's the ugliest building in the city, there is much to discover about this iconic landmark.\n\nJoin us as we explore City Hall’s unique design, its history, and how it serves the people of Boston today. On the tour, we’ll visit the grand ceremonial spaces, the public service areas, and the offices where elected officials and city employees work to make important decisions for our community.\n\nAs we walk through the building, you’ll learn about how its design reflects both the politics and the practicalities of running a city. We’ll discuss how City Hall’s architecture impacts the lives of Boston residents, and invite you to think about how the building works both in everyday life and as a symbol of our city’s values.\n\nBy the end of the tour, you’ll see City Hall in a whole new light and leave with a deeper understanding of its important role in Boston’s story. We hope you’ll feel inspired and connected to this welcoming place that helps shape the future of our city!\n\nThis tour is presented in partnership with the City of Boston.\n\n## Duration, Distance, Terrain\n- 1 hour\n- .5 mile at a moderate pace, stopping at various sites along the tour\n- Mostly flat surfaces and little inclines. \n- Elevators provide access to each floor of City Hall. Please contact us at info@bostonbyfoot.org or 617-367-2345 if you plan to attend this tour and will require accommodations or if you have questions about accessibility. \n\n## Meeting location:\nMeet your guide inside the Government Center MBTA Station station at the entrance/exit facing City Hall\n\nFinding Your Guide: All guides carry an 8×11 sign that says “Boston By Foot Walking Tours.”\n\nNearest MBTA Station: Government Center (Blue and Green lines)\n\n## What to bring\n- All visitors to City Hall must go through security to enter the building. All persons and packages entering the building are subject to search. Firearms, knives, mace, or other weapons are prohibited. \n- Comfortable shoes, dress for the weather, water bottle", "description_text": "", "description_bullets": "", "seo_description": "", "location": "", "booking_notes": "All visitors to City Hall must pass through security and will be subject to metal\ndetector, x-ray, visual, and/or security wand inspections. Individuals who refuse to comply with City Hall’s access procedures will be denied entrance to the building. \n- All visitors are encouraged to review the [City Hall Security Procedures PDF](https://cdn.filestackcontent.com/DDFd91MbQk6SfFTkuXyi)\n- All items brought into City Hall are subject to inspection. Bags and other articles are to be put through the X-ray machine and may be subject to additional visual inspection as\nneeded, including the opening and removal of items. \n- To ensure safety and a swifter entry process, City Hall Property Management strongly discourages guests from bringing large bags into City Hall. \n- Firearms, knives, mace, or other weapons, alcoholic beverages, illegal substances, flammable items, drones and large banners, flags or signs are prohibited. Items that are confiscated by City Hall Property Management will not be returned.", "cancellation_notes": "", "no_transportation_notes": "", "no_transportation_minutes": 15, "headline": "New tour for 2025, exploring the ins and outs of Boston's historic City Hall", "short_description": null, "image_url": "", "image_cdn_url": "", "images": [{"cls": "Image", "uri": "/api/v1/companies/bostonbyfoot/items/523525/images/1133581/", "pk": 1133581, "unicode": "photo", "gallery": "carousel", "image_url": "https://cdn.filestackcontent.com/gG41cnOQfWPfEoJS9U7n", "image_cdn_url": "https://cdn.filestackcontent.com/gG41cnOQfWPfEoJS9U7n", "company": {"cls": "Company", "uri": "/api/v1/com